why we chose stdlib-only http MCP client:
Claude Desktop MCP config GOTCHA — npx race condition (2026-04):

PROBLEM: When configuring multiple MCP servers in claude_desktop_config.json that all use `npx -y mcp-remote` (or any other npx package), Claude Desktop launches them in parallel at startup. They ALL try to install the same package into the shared npm cache simultaneously, causing tar extraction errors:
  npm warn tar TAR_ENTRY_ERROR ENOENT: rename ... -> ....DELETE.xxxx
  'mcp-remote' is not recognized as an internal or external command

Most servers fail to start, only the one that wins the race gets a working install. Inconsistent — different servers succeed each restart.

FIX: Install mcp-remote (and any other shared npx tool) GLOBALLY once, then reference the binary directly in the config:

Step 1: npm install -g mcp-remote
Step 2: Find the install location (Windows: C:\Users\<user>\AppData\Roaming\npm\mcp-remote.cmd, macOS/Linux: $(which mcp-remote))
Step 3: Update config to use the binary path directly:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "qdrant": {
      "command": "C:\\Users\\manni\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\mcp-remote.cmd",
      "args": ["http://192.168.178.2:32775/mcp", "--allow-http", "--transport", "http-only"]
    }
  }
}

Same gotcha applies to ANY shared npx-based MCP server tool — install globally to avoid the cache race.
